==== Serial ====
-> [[docs:techref:hardware:port.serial]] general information about the serial port, serial port cable, etc.

How to connect to the Serial Port of this specific device:\\
{{:media:ea4500_v3_uart.jpg?400|}}

Serial Port is in a socket similar to the one in the [[toh:linksys:ea4500|former versions]].
The socket may be absent on some boards (which may also not have a power switch). In this case, connecting to the exposed soldering holes for the socket also works.

^ PIN   ^ ID         ^
| 1     | Vcc 3.3V   |
| 2     |            |
| 3     | RX         |
| 4     |            |
| 5     | TX         |
| 6     | GND        |

Pin number 1 is the one near the screw hole. The TX pin on the board should be connected to the RX pin of the serial console in order to see what the board is transmitting.  Speed (baud) 115200, Data bits 8, Stop bits 1, Parity none.
